  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Man",
     "texto": [
      "**Man** is an impersonal subject that usually corresponds to «one», «people» or «you», depending on the sentence: **Man skal altid være høflig.** = You always have to be polite. It doesn't automatically match every use of English «one»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Passive with modals",
     "texto": [
      "With a modal (**skal, kan, må**) and the passive you use **gøres** (to be done), **ændres** (to be changed): **Det skal gøres.** = It has to be done. **Det kan ikke gøres i dag.** = It can't be done today.",
      "With **må ikke** = must not: **Det må ikke ændres uden tilladelse.** = It must not be changed without permission."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
